==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ʌnˈfəːl/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ʌnˈfɝl/}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)l}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{nautical}} To [[unroll]] or [[release]], especially a [[sail]] or a [[flag]].
#: ''They '''unfurled''' the flag at the start of the festival.''
# {{figurative}} To [[roll out]] or [[debut]] anything.
#: ''When will we be '''unfurling''' the new feature?''

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|to unroll or release}} [[furl]]

